This project contains no code from AndroMeld (closed source). Its behaviour was inferred only
from AndroMeld's public announcement and help pages.

The technique of running framework code under `adb shell app_process` with a minimal
ActivityThread / shell-identity Context, and of talking to it over an `adb forward`ed local
abstract socket, is the one popularised by scrcpy (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy,
Apache-2.0, Copyright Genymobile and contributors). screen-camera's implementation of that
idea (Env.java, ShellContext.java, FrameServer.java) is independent and reduced; no scrcpy
source files are included.

API shapes of android.companion.virtual.* in server/hidden-api are compile-only stubs written
from the public AOSP sources (Apache-2.0, The Android Open Source Project); they are not
packaged into the server jar.
